# What is tracked here is code and JUDGEMENT. What is ignored is STATE.
#
# The distinction is the one state_sync.sh already makes (see its header): the judgement
# files are weeks of accumulated corrections that cannot be rebuilt from anything, so they
# belong in version control. The state files are caches and running bookkeeping - they are
# rewritten wholesale every morning, they are large, and a diff of them says nothing a human
# would read. They have their own daily backup via `./state_sync.sh push`, so ignoring them
# here loses nothing.

# --- credentials. Never commit these. -----------------------------------------------------
# They normally live outside the repo at ~/.config/breakfast-briefing/, but state_sync.sh
# names them, so guard against a copy ever landing here.
oauth.json
sa.json
*.token
.token
.access_token
.refresh_token

# --- the eight state files (rewritten every run; ~7MB combined) ----------------------------
seen.json
cut.json
source_health.json
resolved.json
authors.json
ledes.json
openings.json
previews.json

# --- per-run output, regenerated by every compose ------------------------------------------
composed.json
expected_urls.txt

# --- generated directories -----------------------------------------------------------------
# markdown backup of each edition, written by compose.py --md
out/
snapshots/
# The ranking-evaluation corpus. Written once per edition and never touched again, ~600KB a
# day, and it already has a purpose-built incremental backup in upload-archive-to-drive.sh.
# Tracking it would put the whole corpus in every clone for no benefit.
archive/

# --- python ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.venv/

# --- editor / OS ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store

# NOT ignored, deliberately - these are the judgement files, and losing them is the failure
# this repo exists to prevent:
#   testcases.txt exclusions.txt bylines.txt link_fixes.txt extra_feeds.txt
#   sources.opml briefing-sources.opml tiers.json rank_eval_log.txt
